}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every suffix of every text ends at a leaf, the empty suffix included, and every internal node"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a point where suffixes that agree so far go different ways, so the tree has at most 2"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":" + 1"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nodes. A pattern is found in O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"m","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":") steps down from the root, and the leaves below where it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ends are its occurrences."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let tree = SuffixTree(\"banana\")","tree.occurrences(of: \"ana\").map(\\.range)   \/\/ [3 ..< 6, 1 ..< 4]","tree.longestRepeatedSubstring?.range       \/\/ 3 ..< 6, \"ana\"","","let both = SuffixTree(texts: [\"xabxac\", \"abcabxabcd\"])","both.longestCommonSubstring                \/\/ text 1, 3 ..< 7: \"abxa\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Nodes are numbered in preorder from the root at 0, so a node’s subtree is the nodes from it to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"just before the next node that is not its descendant. Children come in the order of the symbol","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that starts their edge: sorted when ","type":"text"},{"code":"Symbol","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"Comparable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so the leaves are in the order of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their suffixes and match a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixArray"},{"text":" of the same text; otherwise in the order the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"symbols first occur in the texts. Each text ends in a terminator of its own that sorts before","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every symbol and belongs to no label.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tree converts to Grafluent’s "},{"code":"RootedTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":"RootedTree(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and its suffix links are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a directed graph, "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree\/suffixLinksView-swift.property","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Each node takes 32 bytes and each symbol 4 more, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"texts’ codes, which the tree keeps."}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/suffixstructures\/suffixtree"]}],"references":{"doc://SuffixStructures/documentation/SuffixStructures/SuffixTree/pathLabel(of:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"The symbols on the path from the root to the node, as a place in one of the texts where","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"they occur: for a leaf, its suffix; for an internal node, the occurrence at its first leaf;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for the root, the empty range at the start of the first text.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree\/pathLabel(of:)","title":"pathLabel(of:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"pathLabel"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"of"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdent